{
  "_comment": "Shared corpus for credential masking. scalo-rs holds the source of truth in tests/fixtures/credential_masking_parity.json, and scalo-py vendors it to tests/fixtures/patterns/credential_masking_parity.json. Change a case in scalo-rs first, then run tools/vendor_patterns.sh in scalo-py with a scalo-rs checkout in SCALO_RS_CHECKOUT or ../scalo-rs; its --check mode reports a copy that has drifted. scalo-py (scalo.logger.filters.is_credential_name, mask_url_userinfo, the L2 FieldNameScrubber and the logger's record fields) and scalo-rs (logger::is_credential_name, mask_url_userinfo, mask_sensitive_string with default_sensitive_fields, and the JSON writer) must agree on every entry. Before comparing, replace {mask} with the language's mask token, {secret} with a value built at runtime, {pw} with \"p@\" followed by that value, so no credential-shaped literal sits on disk, and {window} with 4096 copies of x, which carries a Name(...) value past the 4096 bytes it is read within.",
  "_columns": "names: name lists. parent_cases: name, parent, credential. text_cases: input, expected, through the text masker. url_cases: input, mask, keep_user, expected, through mask_url_userinfo. structured_cases: input, expected, a record's fields walked as JSON. coarse_cases: input, should_mask, where only whether the output differs is asserted.",
